# Proposed exact-image managed Auth metadata capture

This file is a proposal, not execution or approval. Stage A completed under Ruling33. A separate controller ruling is required before this stage.

1. PG image: `public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgres@sha256:0450166354dc9c1d25f0322ac8b580774d4fb0184d2b087f6e4fe9499c66cf53`, exact original failed CI log image. Auth image: `public.ecr.aws/supabase/gotrue@sha256:1736a63078f5922b198c4cbe50f80ab9a2d3b54fe8b7b6cfb2e9dc5dbbc12c6b`, same original CI log, already cached.
2. Create a fresh uniquely named PG container on network none, no published ports or host mounts, no persistent volume, CPU1/memory1GiB, no healthcheck. Its writable layer contains its new empty database cluster. Existing Docker engine, stacks, databases, template, roles and settings are untouched.
3. Copy the unmodified official CLI v2.118.0 `schema.sql` (Git blob `dee166ae58a4b1f77b650d8e72f8a249e5918ce5`) to the owned container `/etc/postgresql.schema.sql`, where the exact image entrypoint normally reads it. Synthetic password/JWT environment only. Run the normal exact-image entrypoint. Vendor init scripts establish the fresh cluster; no repository migration, production dump or application rows are used. The copied schema template configures fresh synthetic internal login credentials; it is not applied to any existing instance.
4. Run one short-lived GoTrue `gotrue migrate` job in the new PG container's network namespace (`--network container:<exact owned name>`). It can reach only the isolated PG loopback. Use the six environment entries defined by official exact-version CLI `initAuthJob`: local API/site URLs, log-level error, driver postgres, DB URL for the freshly initialized `supabase_auth_admin`, and dummy JWT. Never start the Auth API, send email, evaluate an actor RPC, call auth.uid, or execute a network-bearing SQL primitive.
5. Full read-only catalog captures before/after managed Auth migrations include all auth/public/private helper pg_proc columns, raw bodies, rendered definitions, defaults/arguments/owner/expanded ACL and grant options, config/language/volatility/strict/parallel/security, trigger/dependency metadata, native/catalog prerequisites, roles/defaults/Auth relation metadata. Query zero Auth-user count only in this new owned empty instance. No business fixtures or helper evaluation.
6. No CLI webhook/_supabase templates, Storage/Realtime migrations or application migrations are included. This is explicitly an exact PG/Auth image component reconstruction, not the original failed runner's full final catalog or a successful full CI bootstrap. Those omitted unrelated steps must not be inferred compatible. No allowance is admitted from a source text comparison alone.
7. Capture all commands, stdout/stderr, raw/canonical hashes, image/runtime IDs, before/after catalog metadata and resource identities. Check ownership/name/state before cleanup; remove the completed Auth job normally. Send SIGINT to only the owned PG container using `docker stop --signal SIGINT --timeout -1` (no SIGKILL timeout fallback). Remove only that stopped container with `docker rm -v`; no force/prune or image deletion. Preserve any failed setup evidence rather than patching grants/defaults/roles to proceed.

Reviewed source observations: the image's initial auth.uid is the older single current_setting form; official GoTrue v2.197.0 migration `20220224000811_update_auth_functions.up.sql` produces the exact LF body seen on modern17.6 (`cdef18c69c4f4cbbced2eaf81e628b49`). Its full final17.11 metadata is not yet captured. Official image initialization creates extension and permission helpers; network helpers remain stored definitions, never invoked, and the fresh network namespace has no external connectivity or scheduled application jobs.
